<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramón Villeda Morales</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1909">1909</a>–<a href="/years/1971">1971</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramón Villeda Morales (1909–1971) was a Honduran physician and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-party-uk">Liberal Party</a> politician who was president from 1957 to 1963. His government introduced a labour code, social security and an agrarian reform law, and created a Civil Guard as a counterweight to the army. Ten days before the 1963 election he was overthrown in a coup led by Colonel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswaldo-lopez-arellano">Oswaldo López Arellano</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramon-villeda-morales.jpg" alt="Ramón Villeda Morales" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Associated Press · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ram%C3%B3n_Villeda_Morales_1962r.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
